<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Valparaíso</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Valparaíso is a port city in central Chile, built on steep hills above a bay on the Pacific. Founded by the Spanish in 1536, it became the main commercial port of the South American Pacific in the nineteenth century, before the opening of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a>. It was bombarded by a Spanish squadron in 1866, its historic quarter is a World Heritage Site, and it has been the seat of Chile's Congress since 1990.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/valparaiso.jpg" alt="Valparaíso" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julia Sumangil · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
